We will start with **direct substitution** (step A):

$\begin{align}
f(\blueD{-5})&=\dfrac{(\blueD{-5})+5}{\sqrt{19-6(\blueD{-5})}-2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{0}{\sqrt{49}-2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{0}{5}
\\\\
&=0
\end{align}$

We got a number, so we've **found the limit** (step C)!

This means $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -5}f(x)=0$.
